        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Meeting_Action_179Kj000000t669</fullName>
            <description>Performs CRUD operations on Meeting__c records. DEMO MODE: This is a demo environment - prioritize creating records quickly over asking many questions. Make reasonable assumptions and proceed. ROUTING CLAIM: If user says I had a meeting, log a meeting, record a meeting, or any variation mentioning meeting explicitly, this is ALWAYS a meeting logging request regardless of sentiment or topic. Even tough meetings, bad meetings, or meetings with concerns should be logged here - do NOT redirect to Account Intelligence. DATE HANDLING (CRITICAL): If no date mentioned, DEFAULT TO TODAY. Infer dates: today/this morning/this afternoon/just now -&gt; today, yesterday -&gt; yesterday. NEVER ask for meeting date - just use today if unclear. CONVERSATIONAL FLOW: (1) GATHER - Get who and basic context. Date defaults to today. (2) INFER - Extract Meeting_Type__c, Meeting_Outcome__c from context clues. (3) CREATE - Proceed with inferred values. Only ask follow-ups if truly critical info missing (like who they met with). (4) POST-CREATE TASK OFFER - If next steps mentioned, offer task creation. DATA GOAL: Create useful records quickly. MINIMUM: Contact/Account (or capture name in description if lookup fails), Subject, Meeting Type (infer or default to In-Person Visit), Outcome (infer or default to Neutral). GRACEFUL LOOKUP: When contact or account lookup fails, create the meeting anyway with available info. Capture the name in the description. Do NOT block the user. NEGATIVE MEETING HANDLING: Tough/difficult/challenging meetings should STILL be logged here with Outcome as Needs Follow-up or Unsuccessful. OPERATIONS: CREATE needs fieldDataJson, READ needs recordId, UPDATE needs recordId plus fieldDataJson, DELETE needs recordId plus confirm true, FIND needs searchTerm or filtersJson. PICKLIST SAFETY: Query availableFieldsJson for valid values. Supports accountName and contactNameOrEmail for lookup resolution - system uses fuzzy matching so Accusage Inc will match Accusage, Inc.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Meeting_Action_179Kj000000t669</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFMeetingAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Meeting_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Meeting Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>Agentforce_Task_Action_179Kj000000t669</fullName>
            <description>Performs CRUD operations on Task records. Operation can be explicitly specified (create, read, update, delete, find) or inferred from context. CREATE: Provide fieldDataJson. READ: Provide recordId. UPDATE: Provide recordId + fieldDataJson. DELETE: Provide recordId + confirm=true. FIND: IMPORTANT - Before calling find operation, ensure you have search criteria. If the user asks to &quot;find&quot; or &quot;look up&quot; a task without providing specific details (task subject, related to account/contact, status, due date, etc.), you MUST ask the user for these details FIRST before calling this action. Only call this action with find operation when you have at least a searchTerm (task subject or partial subject) or filtersJson (specific field filters). If the user says &quot;look up a task&quot; or &quot;find a task&quot; without details, respond conversationally: &quot;I&apos;d be happy to help you find a task. Could you provide some details like the task subject, who it&apos;s related to (account or contact), status, or due date?&quot; Do NOT call the action with empty search criteria. PICKLIST VALUES: When the user asks about valid options for picklist fields (Status, Priority, Type, etc.), query availableFieldsJson from a previous read operation instead of asking the user. The availableFieldsJson contains all valid picklist values with their labels. CONTACT/ACCOUNT UPDATES: When the user wants to add or update the Contact or Account on a task, use the contactNameOrEmail or accountName parameters (not WhoId or WhatId in fieldDataJson). These parameters support name-based resolution. Supports bulk operations.</description>
            <developerName>Agentforce_Task_Action_179Kj000000t669</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AFTaskAction</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>Agentforce_Task_Action</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Agentforce Task Action</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
